-- title:
--   Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation at fine level, tower and Atkin–Lehner
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $\mathcal{O}$ plays the role of the ring of integers of an unramified $r$-adic base, $\widehat{\mathcal{O}}^{\mathrm{nr}}$ is modelled by `Onr`, and the formal upper half plane is modelled by the functor `Omega K₀ π` of Deligne data.
--
--   **Numerical data.** Primes $r$ and $\bar r$ with $\bar r \neq r$, and a nonzero natural number $N$ with $r \nmid N$, $\bar r \nmid N$ and $N$ squarefree.
--
--   **The base ring.** A characteristic-zero commutative domain $\mathcal{O}$ which is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`), in which $2$ and $3$ are units, together with an irreducible element $\pi$ such that $\mathcal{O}$ is $\pi$-adically complete, $\#(\mathcal{O}/(\pi)) = r$, and $(r) = (\pi)$; and a characteristic-zero field $K_0$ which is a fraction field of $\mathcal{O}$.
--
--   **The unramified cover and Frobenius.** A characteristic-zero commutative domain $\mathrm{Onr}$ with an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra structure and an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra automorphism $\mathrm{Fr}$, subject to: $\mathrm{Onr}$ is adically complete for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$; that ideal is maximal; every element of $\mathrm{Onr}$ satisfies, modulo $\pi$, a monic polynomial over $\mathcal{O}$ (`hOnr_alg`); every monic polynomial of positive degree over $\mathrm{Onr}$ has a root modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_closed`); and $\mathrm{Fr}(x) \equiv x^{r} \pmod{\pi}$ for all $x$. Further, a monoid homomorphism $\mathrm{vdet} : \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0) \to \mathbb{Z}$ (written multiplicatively) characterised by `hvdet`: $\mathrm{vdet}(g) = n$ if and only if $\det g = u\,\pi^{n}$ for some $u \in \mathcal{O}^{\times}$.
--
--   **The indefinite side and the coarse moduli scheme.** Rationals $a, b$ with `IsIndefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt a b r rbar`, that is, $0 < a$ or $0 < b$, and for every finite place $v$ of $\mathbb{Q}$ the completion $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b] \otimes \mathbb{Q}_v$ is a division algebra exactly when $v$ lies over $r$ or over $\bar r$; a maximal order $\Lambda$ (an order not properly contained in any order); a scheme $\mathcal{X}$ with a morphism $f$ to $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal{O}$ and a point assignment $\mathrm{pt}$ sending a fake elliptic curve with level-$N$ structure over an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra $S$ to an $S$-point of $\mathcal{X}$, such that `h𝒳 : IsCoarseModuli Λ N 𝒳 f pt` holds: $\mathrm{pt}$ is constant on isomorphism classes, compatible with base change along ring maps, bijective on isomorphism classes over algebraically closed fields, and initial among all such families. In addition the generic fibre, the second projection of the pullback of $f$ along $\operatorname{Spec} K_0 \to \operatorname{Spec}\mathcal{O}$, is geometrically reduced and geometrically connected.
--
--   **The auxiliary fine level.** A natural number $n \geq 3$ with $r \nmid n$, $\bar r \nmid n$ and $\gcd(n,N) = 1$; a scheme $M$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal{O}$ with structure morphism $f_M$ and a point assignment $\mathrm{ptF}$ on pairs (fake elliptic curve with level-$N$ structure, full level-$n$ structure), with `hM : IsFineModuli Λ N n M fM ptF`: $\mathrm{ptF}$ is constant on isomorphism classes, compatible with base change, and bijective on such pairs over every $\mathcal{O}$-algebra. A group $G$ with $\rho : G \to \operatorname{Aut} M$ and $\chi : G \to \Lambda$ satisfying `hρ : IsLevelTwistAction`: each $\rho(g)$ lies over the base, twisting the full level structure by $\chi(g)$ is realised by post-composition with $\rho(g)$, $\chi$ is multiplicative and unital modulo $n$, and $\chi$ induces a bijection from $G$ onto the classes of elements of $\Lambda$ invertible modulo $n$.
--
--   **The forgetful morphism.** A morphism $p : M \to \mathcal{X}$ with $p$ followed by $f$ equal to $f_M$, invariant under all $\rho(h)$, and such that $\mathrm{ptF}(S,s,u)$ followed by $p$ is $\mathrm{pt}(S,s,u_1)$ for every pair $u$ with underlying curve $u_1$.
--
--   **The Hecke tower.** For every prime $\ell \notin \{r, \bar r\}$ (the type `HeckeTower.AwayPrime r rbar`), a scheme $\mathcal{Y}_\ell$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal{O}$ with structure morphism $g_\ell$ and a point assignment $\mathrm{ptT}_\ell$ on fake elliptic curves equipped with an extra level-$\ell$ subgroup (a finite flat $\Lambda$-stable closed subgroup of rank $\ell^2$, killed by $\ell$, disjoint from the level-$N$ structure, with geometric fibres isomorphic to $(\mathbb{Z}/\ell)^2$), such that `IsCoarseModuliT` holds for each $\ell$ (the analogue of `IsCoarseModuli` for these pairs), each generic fibre being geometrically reduced and geometrically connected. Degeneracy morphisms $d_0(\ell), d_1(\ell) : \mathcal{Y}_\ell \to \mathcal{X}$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal{O}$ are given, with $d_0(\ell)$ sending the point of a pair to the point of its underlying curve, and $d_1(\ell)$ sending it to the point of any curve $d$ for which `FakeEllipticCurve.IsLevelIsogeny ℓ u d` holds, i.e. $d$ is the quotient by the extra level subgroup in the sense of a pair of $\Lambda$-equivariant isogenies composing to multiplication by $\ell$ with prescribed kernel.
--
--   **Atkin–Lehner morphisms.** Endomorphisms $a_r$ and $a_{\bar r}$ of $\mathcal{X}$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal{O}$ such that $\mathrm{pt}(E)$ followed by $a_r$ equals $\mathrm{pt}(E')$ whenever `FakeEllipticCurve.IsAtkinLehnerQuotient r E E'`, and likewise for $a_{\bar r}$ at $\bar r$.
--
--   **The definite side.** Rationals $a_1, b_1$ with `IsDefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt rbar`: $a_1 < 0$, $b_1 < 0$, and $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a_1,b_1] \otimes \mathbb{Q}_v$ is a division algebra exactly at the place over $\bar r$. A maximal order $\Lambda_1$ and an Eichler order $R_1$ of level $N$ (an intersection of two maximal orders of relative index $N$) with $R_1 \leq \Lambda_1$; a unit $n_1$ of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a_1,b_1] \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} \mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q},\mathrm{fin}}$ lying in `primeHeckeSet R₁ r` (that is, $n_1$ lies in the adelic box of $R_1$, so does $r\,n_1^{-1}$, while $n_1^{-1}$ and $r^{-1}n_1$ do not), such that $R_1 \cap n_1 R_1 n_1^{-1}$ (`meetOrder R₁ n₁`) is an Eichler order of level $Nr$; an injective $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra homomorphism $\iota_0 : \mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a_1,b_1] \to M_2(K_0)$; and the height-one prime $v$ of the integers of $\mathbb{Q}$ containing $r$.
--
--   **The discrete group and the Hecke elements.** A subgroup $\tilde\Gamma$ of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a_1,b_1]^{\times}$ characterised by `hΓt` as [`CerednikDrinfeld.CosetGraph.awayUnits R₁ v`](def/CerednikDrinfeld_CosetGraphAtPrime.html#L37): the elements whose image in the completion at $w$ lies in the subgroup generated by the local unit box of $R_1$ at $w$, for every finite place $w \neq v$. For each $\ell$ away from $r,\bar r$, elements $s_\ell \in \mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a_1,b_1]^{\times}$ and adelic units $sf_\ell$ with `hs`: $sf_\ell$ has component $s_\ell$ at every place not over $r$, component $1$ at the places over $r$, the product of the diagonal image of $\ell$ with $sf_\ell^{-1}$ lies in `levelHeckeUSet Λ₁ (meetOrder R₁ n₁) ℓ` when $\ell \mid N$ and in `primeHeckeSet (meetOrder R₁ n₁) ℓ` otherwise, and the reduced norm of $s_\ell$ equals $\ell$. Finally $\tilde\Gamma_\ell = \tilde\Gamma \cap s_\ell \tilde\Gamma s_\ell^{-1}$.
--
--   **The Atkin–Lehner element.** A unit $\bar w$ of reduced norm $\bar r$ normalising $\tilde\Gamma$, and such that $r^{k}\bar w \in R_1$ for some $k \in \mathbb{N}$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** There exist a group homomorphism $\theta_t : \tilde\Gamma \to G$, a family
--   $$\Theta_f : \bigl((\mathrm{Onr} \to_{\mathcal{O}} B) \times \Omega(B)\bigr) \times G \longrightarrow (\mathrm{nilpPoints}\,f_M)(B),$$
--   defined for every $\mathcal{O}$-algebra $B$ in which the image of $\pi$ is nilpotent, and, for each $\ell$ away from $r,\bar r$, a family
--   $$\Theta_T^{(\ell)} : (\mathrm{Onr} \to_{\mathcal{O}} B) \times \Omega(B) \longrightarrow (\mathrm{nilpPoints}\,g_\ell)(B),$$
--   where $\Omega(B) =$ `(Omega K₀ π).obj B` is the set of Deligne data over $B$ (an assignment to each full $\mathcal{O}$-lattice $M \subset K_0^2$ of a $B$-submodule of $B \otimes_{\mathcal{O}} M$ with invertible quotient, monotone in $M$, equivariant for homotheties, and nondegenerate at every prime of $B$) and $(\mathrm{nilpPoints}\,h)(B)$ is the set of morphisms $\operatorname{Spec} B \to$ (source of $h$) over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal{O}$, such that the following thirteen groups of clauses hold.
--
--   (i) $\Theta_f$ is natural: for every $\mathcal{O}$-algebra homomorphism $\varphi : B \to B'$ between rings in which $\pi$ is nilpotent, $\Theta_f$ of the image of $x$ equals the image under $\varphi$ of $\Theta_f(x)$.
--
--   (ii) $G$-equivariance: post-composition with $\rho(h)$ (a morphism over the base by `hρ.over_base`) sends $\Theta_f(x, gh)$ to $\Theta_f(x, g)$, for all $g, h \in G$.
--
--   (iii) $\tilde\Gamma$-invariance: for $\gamma \in \tilde\Gamma$ and $x, x'$ with `OmegaNr.IsTwistedAct π Onr Fr vdet B (ι₀ γ) x x'`, that is $x'_1 = x_1 \circ \mathrm{Fr}^{-\mathrm{vdet}(\iota_0\gamma)}$ and $x'_2$ is the pullback of $x_2$ along $(\iota_0\gamma)^{-1}$, one has $\Theta_f(x', \theta_t(\gamma)g) = \Theta_f(x, g)$.
--
--   (iv) Formal étaleness: for a surjective $\mathcal{O}$-algebra homomorphism $B \to B_0$ between rings in which $\pi$ is nilpotent whose kernel is square-zero (any two elements mapping to $0$ have product $0$), and for $x_0$ over $B_0$ and $y \in (\mathrm{nilpPoints}\,f_M)(B)$ whose image in $(\mathrm{nilpPoints}\,f_M)(B_0)$ is $\Theta_f(x_0)$, there is a unique $x$ over $B$ lifting $x_0$ with $\Theta_f(x) = y$.
--
--   (v) Geometric points: for every algebraically closed field $k$ which is an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra with $\pi$ nilpotent and every $\psi : \mathrm{Onr} \to_{\mathcal{O}} k$, every $y \in (\mathrm{nilpPoints}\,f_M)(k)$ is of the form $\Theta_f((\psi, P), g)$ for some Deligne datum $P$ and some $g \in G$; and $\Theta_f((\psi,P),g) = \Theta_f((\psi',P'),g')$ holds if and only if there is $\gamma \in \tilde\Gamma$ with $g' = \theta_t(\gamma)g$, with $P'$ the pullback of $P$ along $(\iota_0\gamma)^{-1}$ in the sense of `DeligneDatum.IsPullback`, and with $\psi'(y) = (\psi \circ \mathrm{Fr}^{-\mathrm{vdet}(\iota_0\gamma)})(y)$ for every $y \in \mathrm{Onr}$ that is fixed by $\mathrm{Fr}^{\mathrm{vdet}(\iota_0 z)}$ for all scalar $z \in \tilde\Gamma$ (that is, $z = c \cdot 1$ with $c \in \mathbb{Q}$) with $\theta_t(z) = 1$.
--
--   (vi) Universality of $\Theta_f$: for every scheme $T$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal{O}$ and every family $\rho'$ on the same source functor which is natural in $B$ and satisfies the $\tilde\Gamma$-invariance of clause (iii), there is a natural transformation $u$ from $\mathrm{nilpPoints}\,f_M$ to $\mathrm{nilpPoints}$ of the structure morphism of $T$ with $u \circ \Theta_f = \rho'$, and any natural $u'$ with $u' \circ \Theta_f = \rho'$ agrees with $u$ on all such $B$.
--
--   (vii) Each $\Theta_T^{(\ell)}$ is natural in $B$.
--
--   (viii) Each $\Theta_T^{(\ell)}$ is invariant under the twisted action of $\iota_0\gamma$ for $\gamma \in \tilde\Gamma_\ell$.
--
--   (ix) Geometric points in the tower: for $k$ algebraically closed as above and $\psi$ fixed, every point of $(\mathrm{nilpPoints}\,g_\ell)(k)$ is $\Theta_T^{(\ell)}(\psi, P)$ for some $P$, and $\Theta_T^{(\ell)}(\psi,P) = \Theta_T^{(\ell)}(\psi,P')$ if and only if some $\gamma \in \tilde\Gamma_\ell$ carries $(\psi,P)$ to $(\psi,P')$ under the twisted action of $\iota_0\gamma$.
--
--   (x) Universality of each $\Theta_T^{(\ell)}$, in the same form as (vi) with $\tilde\Gamma_\ell$-invariance in place of $\tilde\Gamma$-invariance.
--
--   (xi) Compatibility with $d_0$: post-composition with $d_0(\ell)$ applied to $\Theta_T^{(\ell)}(x)$ equals post-composition with $p$ applied to $\Theta_f(x, 1)$.
--
--   (xii) Compatibility with $d_1$: if $x$ is obtained from $x'$ by the twisted action of $\iota_0(s_\ell)$, then post-composition with $d_1(\ell)$ applied to $\Theta_T^{(\ell)}(x)$ equals post-composition with $p$ applied to $\Theta_f(x', 1)$.
--
--   (xiii) Atkin–Lehner at $r$ and at $\bar r$: post-composition with $a_r$ sends the image under $p$ of $\Theta_f(x,1)$ to the image under $p$ of $\Theta_f((x_1 \circ \mathrm{Fr},\, x_2), 1)$; and if $x'$ is obtained from $x$ by the twisted action of $\iota_0(\bar w)$, then post-composition with $a_{\bar r}$ sends the image under $p$ of $\Theta_f(x,1)$ to the image under $p$ of $\Theta_f(x',1)$.
--
--   This is the Čerednik–Drinfeld $r$-adic uniformisation in its linked fine-level form: the formal completion along the special fibre of the auxiliary fine-level model $M$, and of each tower scheme $\mathcal{Y}_\ell$, is presented as a quotient of $\widehat{\Omega} \times (\mathrm{Onr}\text{-points})$ by the arithmetic group $\tilde\Gamma$ attached to an Eichler order in the definite quaternion algebra ramified at $\bar r$, compatibly with the degeneracy maps of the Hecke tower and with the Atkin–Lehner involutions at $r$ and at $\bar r$. It is the fine-level input to the corresponding coarse-level uniformisation statement, from which the description of the reduction of the Shimura curve and its Hecke and Atkin–Lehner structure at $r$ is obtained.
